        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162419614?u=2b6e602f394a737b5c7baed1bfb34376d6de6b78&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;canvas&gt;</code> element ID used in the Path2D examples.<br>\nThe previous examples used <code class=\"notranslate\">id=\"canvas\"</code>, which can lead beginners to accidentally use a non-canvas element with the same ID, resulting in the common error:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">getContext is not a function</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The examples now consistently use <code class=\"notranslate\">id=\"myCanvas\"</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Using a more specific and less generic ID helps prevent confusion for new developers.<br>\nIt avoids accidental misuse of <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;div id=\"canvas\"&gt;</code> and improves the clarity and reliability of the example code.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Updated the HTML <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;canvas&gt;</code> ID in both examples.</li>\n<li>Updated corresponding JavaScript <code class=\"notranslate\">getElementById()</code> calls.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42155.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3673193420\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42155\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42155/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42155\">#42155</a></p>",
