        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25124?u=30f795781471e611f63aefdfcf39f523b0e22ca3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Rewrote html / javascript examples for consistency, added consistent log output.</li>\n<li>Added examples of <code class=\"notranslate\">returnValue</code> in close and requestClose</li>\n<li>Added additional context around close requests (linking out to spec) and cancel events</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The examples are now much simpler focussing on the api methods. I've removed a lot of form related cruft which may have been confusing to developers new to the APIs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm pretty sure the examples were originally copied from <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog#examples\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog#examples</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If this PR is successful I'll start on consolidating the examples in the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog</a> docs.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After finding a broken example in the docs (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3654512971\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42053\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42053/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42053\">#42053</a>) I found more inconsistencies in the examples across all the Web APIs / HTMLDialogElement docs.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Questions for reviewers… this is my first major PR.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a style guide for when to use links vs code blocks for api methods in related docs? I've seen examples of both <code class=\"notranslate\">returnValue</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">{{domxref(\"HTMLDialogElement.returnValue\", \"returnValue\")}}</code>, and {{domxref(\"HTMLDialogElement.returnValue\")}}.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a style guide for writing code examples? In this case I've stuck with id selectors from the first example I updated, this also makes selection a bit clearer for new developers IMO, but it also may set a bad precedent.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Should the details page for a property include more information that the property on the element page. Example: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog#closedby\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog#closedby</a> contained more information about how the property worked than the instance property: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogElement/closedBy\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogElement/closedBy</a>. Should these docs be rewritten to reflect each other?</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3654512971\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42053\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42053/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42053\">#42053</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">// ping <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hamishwillee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hamishwillee\">@hamishwillee</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42127",
            "title": "Revise: Web APIs / HTMLDialogElement Docs",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-02T08:49:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-26T12:01:20.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "leevigraham",
                "url": "https://github.com/leevigraham"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;meta name=\"rating\"&gt;</code> element, supported behind prefs for now. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991135\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991135</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a section covering it to the Firefox Experimental Features page, and adds a short note to the Experimental Web Features section of the Fx146 rel notes page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I didn't think this required BCD adding or coverage in the main HTML reference yet, given that it is not supported anywhere by default at the moment. Let me know if you think I <em>should</em> add these.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42119",
            "title": "Firefox 146 support for <meta name=rating>",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-25T17:17:09.000Z",
