            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is still in DRAFT mode!!!!</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42105",
            "title": "DRAFT: CSS scroll driven animation guide: range insets",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-01T15:36:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-25T11:11:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 142 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">:target-before</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">:target-after</code> pseudo classes. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5120827674722304\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5120827674722304</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds reference docs for the new pseudos, and adds mention and coverage of them in appropriate places.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42103",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document :target-before and :target-after pseudos",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-26T17:20:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-25T08:50:31.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 142 adds support for range syntax in style queries, both in CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">if()</code>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184992749289472\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184992749289472</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-chrome-142#range-syntax\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-chrome-142#range-syntax</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds content about style query range syntax to both the <code class=\"notranslate\">if()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> reference pages, and coverage to the size/style container queries guide.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note: Usage of substitution functions like <code class=\"notranslate\">attr()</code> in range style queries didn't seem to work, in my testing, for example:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\".item-grid {\n  background-color: if(style(attr(data-columns, type&lt;number&gt;) &gt; 2): lightblue; else: white);\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">.<span class=\"pl-c1\">item-grid</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">background-color</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">if</span>(<span class=\"pl-en\">style</span>(<span class=\"pl-en\">attr</span>(data-columns<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> type&lt;number&gt;) <span class=\"pl-c1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>)<span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> lightblue; else: white);\n}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've left a mention of it in the docs, but I should probably remove it and update the associated <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28510\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28510/hovercard\">browser compat data</a> if these don't work at the moment.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If they do work, can you provide me with an example that works, so I can see what I'm doing wrong?</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41982.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3633946647\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41982\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41982/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41982\">#41982</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42082",
            "title": "Technical review: Add information on if()/container style query range syntax",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-24T14:01:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-24T13:43:05.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The worker constructor takes a <code class=\"notranslate\">url</code> parameter that that can be a <code class=\"notranslate\">TrustedScriptURL</code>. This attempts to follow the pattern of our other trusted types docs and add the header warning and security considerations section.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note this is draft because I am trying to tidy up other inconsistencies with the documentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related project: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
